reflection and next steps ( chatgpt)


Add caching for company news.
Fetching Google News per job can get expensive and noisy. Cache by company for a short window and store a “news freshness” timestamp. That will reduce repeated lookups and keep the UI snappy.  


Measure the system.
Useful metrics would be:

click-through rate on jobs
save/apply rate
average rank of clicked jobs
precision at top 10
profile extraction completeness
latency per stage
12:50 PM
All truncation in this codebase is logging-only — _truncate(300 chars) and user_message[:200] only affect what's printed to the console. The actual data sent to the LLM is always the full content.

Job results — limited by count (per_page, default 5–10), not KB. The full job payload goes into the LLM's context window as tool result messages.

News results — capped at max_results=5 articles per company (google_news_client.py:19). Each item is small (title + source + date + url), so no KB concern.

Resume / free text — no size limit in the code. The practical ceiling is the LLM provider's context window:
- Gemini 2.5 Flash: ~1M tokens (~750K words) — resume size is irrelevant
- Groq Llama-3.3-70b: 128K tokens (~96KB of plain text) — also more than enough for any resume

The one real limit: MAX_TOKENS = 8192 is the output token budget (agent_loop.py:12). This is what the agent uses for its final JSON response and its tool calls. If the agent has fetched many jobs with long descriptions and extensive news, the 8192-token output cap could truncate the final JSON — which is why Gemini's thinking tokens are disabled (they'd eat into this budget without adding value for a structured JSON task).

